        "q": "You are a documentation manager at a bank. How do you manage documentation across multiple product lines that have different teams, different timelines, and different customer audiences?",
        "a": "Managing documentation across multiple product lines in a bank is a portfolio management challenge that requires both centralized governance and decentralized execution. Attempting full centralization produces documentation that is slow and disconnected from product teams; attempting full decentralization produces inconsistency and redundancy.\n\nGovernance model:\n\nI establish centralized governance for standards — the style guide, the content model, the toolset, the publication process, and the review and approval workflow. These standards apply across all product lines and are maintained by the central documentation team. This consistency makes the bank's documentation coherent to customers who interact with multiple products.\n\nExecution model:\n\nEach product line has a documentation owner — either a dedicated technical writer embedded in or closely aligned to the product team, or a product team member trained on documentation standards. This distributed ownership means documentation stays current with product changes without requiring the central team to be the bottleneck for all updates.\n\nAudience-specific content:\n\nDifferent product lines in a bank often serve different customer audiences — retail banking customers differ from private banking customers, differ from business banking customers. The documentation for each audience should be written at the appropriate level of sophistication and use the appropriate vocabulary. A central documentation team helps maintain this audience differentiation consistently across product lines.\n\nShared content library:\n\nSome content is common across product lines — security guidance, the bank's complaint procedure, regulatory disclosure language. I maintain a shared content library for these reusable elements so that the same information appears consistently across all product lines and needs to be updated only once when it changes.\n\nCross-product coordination:\n\nFor product changes that affect multiple product lines simultaneously — a regulatory change, a platform upgrade, a rebranding — I coordinate the documentation update across all affected product lines through a shared project plan with explicit owners and deadlines for each workstream.",
